# mux.snc — Multi-Agent Workflow Orchestration Plan

> **Status:** Proposed architecture and implementation roadmap  
> **Version:** 0.1 (planning draft)  
> **Primary approach:** CLI-first agents + reusable Skills + tmux user interface + a deterministic workflow engine  
> **Project:** mux.snc

## 1. Executive summary

Extend **mux.snc** from a manager of multiple AI-agent terminal sessions into a **provider-neutral, stage-driven workflow orchestrator**. A user submits a task; mux.snc selects a predefined workflow; specialized agents execute stages sequentially or concurrently; validated artifacts carry context between stages; and a persistent scheduler enforces dependencies, retries, security policy, and human approval gates.

**Fundamental design rule:** **Agents perform work; mux.snc controls the workflow.** An agent cannot unilaterally mark a stage as verified, bypass approval, or launch arbitrary downstream stages.

### Desired experience

```bash
mux workflow list
mux workflow validate workflows/feature-development.yaml
mux workflow run feature-development --task "Build a Rust Jira Data Center CLI"
mux workflow status <run-id>
mux workflow graph <run-id>
mux workflow logs <run-id> --stage implementation --follow
mux workflow approve <run-id> --stage approval
mux workflow resume <run-id>
mux workflow cancel <run-id>
```

> The commands, configuration formats, and file paths in this document are **proposals**, not claims about features already implemented in mux.snc.

