```mermaid
flowchart TB
    U[User / CLI] --> M["mux.snc Control Plane"]
    M --> W[Workflow Loader and Validator]
    M --> S["Scheduler / DAG Executor"]
    S <--> DB[(SQLite Run State)]
    S <--> ART[(Run Artifacts)]
    S --> P[Prompt and Context Builder]
    P --> AM[Agent Manager]
    AM --> C[Claude CLI Adapter]
    AM --> G[Copilot CLI Adapter]
    AM --> X[Custom CLI Adapter]
    AM --> T[tmux Session Manager]
    C --> R[Structured Result + Logs]
    G --> R
    X --> R
    R --> V[Output and Policy Validation]
    V --> ART
    V --> S
    S --> H{Approval Required?}
    H -->|Yes| A[Human Approval Gate]
    A --> S
    H -->|No| S
    S --> OBS[Events / Logs / Metrics / Traces]
```

### Responsibility boundaries

| Component | Responsibility | MVP implementation |
|---|---|---|
| Workflow loader | Parse YAML, validate schema, detect cycles and missing dependencies | Static workflows only |
| DAG scheduler | Determine eligible stages and enforce concurrency limits | Single local scheduler |
| Run state store | Transactional states, attempts, leases, artifacts, approval events | SQLite |
| Prompt/context builder | Assemble instructions and verified artifact references | Template + manifest |
| Agent adapters | Start, observe, cancel, and normalize CLI agent runs | Start with one provider |
| Artifact store | Persist outputs and metadata for each run/stage | Local filesystem |
| Validation | Schema checks, exit status, file existence, external commands | Configured validators |
| Policy/approval | Gate privileged actions and final PR creation | CLI approval first |
| tmux presentation | Expose agent panes and run status | UI projection, not state source |
| Telemetry | Structured events, timings, optional token/cost accounting | JSONL logs + metrics |

### Important implementation boundary

Do **not** use terminal text scraping as the source of truth for whether an agent finished. Prefer supported structured CLI/SDK output, controlled subprocess lifecycles, validated output artifacts, and explicit exit/result handling. tmux is excellent for visibility and manual intervention but is not the authoritative workflow database.

