## 14. Risks and mitigations

| Risk | Impact | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|
| CLI provider interface changes | Agent runs fail | Versioned adapters, contract tests |
| Agent output is nondeterministic | Broken handoff | Explicit schemas and validation |
| Parallel mutation races | Lost changes | Immutable snapshots, isolated worktrees |
| Retry loops consume tokens | Runaway cost | Max attempts, budgets, approval escalation |
| Inaccurate token figures | Misleading benchmarks | Null when unsupported; record measurement source |
| Stale approvals | Unauthorized publication | Bind approvals to revision and digest |
| tmux session disappears | Apparent lost execution | DB is source of truth; reconcile process state |
| Untrusted prompts/tools | Data loss or secret exposure | Least privilege, allowlists, sandboxes, human gates |

